# Kernel source pin. kernel/build.sh reads the five fields below; CI's upstream-watch reads
# `version:`. Everything else here is notes for the next bump and the next HW gate.
#
# Current: 7.3.4, pinned 2026-11-13 (issue #42). Builds; not booted yet. The per-board HW gate
# for the 7.3 series is not finished (see "7.3.x on hardware" below).
version:    7.3.4
url:        https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v7.x/linux-7.3.4.tar.xz
sha256:     b11b6df8295e8e991ff040b71aaa4994a8b55caa23b6b092907f195b5840fd1f
git_tag:    v7.3.4
git_commit: 7595a62d45ee1a2297eafa5f2ef5d0a45142d84d

# ============================== The fields ==============================
#
# sha256 comes from kernel.org's signed sha256sums.asc for v7.x, not from hashing what the CDN
# served (that only proves the CDN agrees with itself). The .asc carries a good signature from the
# "Kernel.org checksum autosigner" key, B886 8C80 BA62 A1FF FAF5 FDA9 632D 3A06 589D A6B1 (fetch
# it by WKD or from keyserver.ubuntu.com; keys.openpgp.org serves it without user IDs and gpg then
# reports "no public key"). That key has no trust path here, so the check that counts is
# continuity: the same signed file still lists the pins we shipped before with the hashes we
# recorded. Re-checked 2026-11-13:
#   7.3.3   79c66dde66cd96877fcde8f7d36aec946b1f423d2b97b5a7b1751b75c764f3d1
#   7.3.1   fa595aad93734f829c963c2a90ef7c3673224fd7fdae7b49406e397cde2de231
#   7.2.11  fd0fc479f983a8c05313f13e9c36330fe6651cf725396748c40d5cd93fa1e6a4
# On each bump, add the outgoing pin and drop the oldest; three is enough for a chain.
#
# git_commit is the dereferenced tag (`git ls-remote origin 'v<version>^{}'`), not the annotated
# tag object, which has a different sha. Resolving the previous pin's tag and getting back the
# git_commit it records is a cheap way to check you dereferenced.

# ============================== Pin history ==============================
#
# One line per pin. Details of older pins are in git history (`git log -p kernel/SOURCE.pin`),
# details of each patch in its own header and in kernel/patches/README.md.
#
#   7.0.11  2026-06-17  first validated pin.
#   7.1.5   2026-07-25  HW: Pocket S2, Pocket ACE.
#   7.1.6   2026-08-03
#   7.2     2026-08-18  mainline; took over two of ours (sm8550 bandwidth scaling, sgm3804; see
#                       "What 7.2 took over" below).
#   7.2.1   2026-08-27
#   7.2.3   2026-09-03
#   7.2.4   2026-09-08
#   7.2.5   2026-09-11  issue #91: needed a DSI byte-clock fix to keep two boards' panels alive
#                       (landed upstream in 7.2.8).
#   7.2.6   2026-09-17  skipped on 2026-09-14 (issue #95): Wi-Fi dead on every WCN7850 board and
#                       only half of the Pocket S2's bonded panel drawing. Re-taken with the
#                       pcie-qcom BDF-to-SID fix (now 1060) and a bonded-DSI fix (now 0440).
#                       HW: ACE, S2, Max.
#   7.2.7   2026-09-22  HW: ACE, Thor Lite, FIT.
#   7.2.8   2026-09-27  two of ours landed (DSI byte clock, DPU peripheral flush). HW: ACE, FIT,
#                       S2, Max, plus sustained GPU load on Max.
#   7.2.9   2026-10-03  HW: ACE, S2.
#   7.2.10  2026-10-12  issue #112. HW: ACE, S2, Max (with 0330 v4, 1150, 0140).
#   7.2.11  2026-10-15  no HW gate run before 7.3.1 replaced it.
#   7.3.1   2026-10-30  new series: ten of ours landed and were deleted, the rest rebased.
#   7.3.3   2026-11-08  issue #37: nothing of ours landed, no patch changed.
#   7.3.4   2026-11-13  issue #42: 0896 landed and was deleted, 0975 regenerated, 1166 now
#                       load-bearing.
#
# A point release inside a series is a prediction about effort, never about risk: 7.2.5 needed a
# new patch and 7.2.6 broke Wi-Fi, and both were found on hardware, not by an offline gate.

# ============================== 7.3.4 ==============================
#
# 1254 commits, 1138 files. No qcom dts/dtsi we include moved (only ipq9574, shikra, sdm845
# boards), no dt-bindings header, no adreno or DPU commit; the one drm/msm change we build is a
# DSI VM leak fix. Ported from Nova-Deck 0e44aa0e, re-measured here: sha256 from the signed .asc
# above, git_commit from `git ls-remote ... 'v7.3.4^{}'` (and 'v7.3.3^{}' gives back the old pin).
#
# Landed: 0896 (Val Packett, q6afe clk vote response type), stable f3c7bee984aa. It reversed at
# --fuzz=0 against pristine 7.3.4 and was deleted. Upstream does not carry it, so this is ours
# alone: SM6115 and SM8250 vote the LPASS core clocks through q6afe.
#
# Load-bearing now: 1166. Stable took "misc: fastrpc: Allocate entire reserved memory for Audio PD
# in probe" (827cf4797be4) without the two "Make ADSP remote heaps no-map" dts patches. The driver
# assigns the whole ADSP remote heap to the DSP at rpmsg probe whenever the region is declared and
# the node has qcom,vmids: our SM8250 and SM8750 ADSP nodes. 1166 makes those pages no-map; keep
# it until v7.4. SM4450, SM6115, SM8550 and SM8650 declare no remote heap.
#
# Regenerated: 0975 (fastrpc interrupted invokes). The same fastrpc commit replaced the channel's
# `remote_heap` with remote_heap_addr/_size, which two of 0975's hunks had as context. The +/- lines
# are unchanged; the regenerated patch on pristine 7.3.4 gives the same file as the hand-fixed one.
#
# Intersection with our patches, 21 files, all read:
#   ufs/core/ufshcd.c (1086)       abort/eh_timed_out/clear_lu_cmds double release and completion
#                                  fixes, a clock-scaling vs device-command deadlock, stale UIC
#                                  result byte cleared before peer DME retries.
#   qdsp6 q6apm.c (0897), q6apm-dai.c (0854, 0860), q6asm-dai.c (0880), q6afe.c (0895)
#                                  a full ring's position wraps to 0 (q6apm-dai + q6asm-dai), hw
#                                  pointer reset with the fragment queue, three DSP-buffer unmap
#                                  fixes; q6afe is 0896's landing. The q6apm-dai pointer change is
#                                  on the path after 0854's push-pull branch, i.e. not the
#                                  playback path we use since push-pull.
#   lpass-wsa-macro.c (0855)       Compander1 CTL3/CTL7 at the v2.5 addresses on v2.5+ silicon, in
#                                  wsa_macro_set_spkr_mode(); 0855 only adds sleep handlers.
#   fastrpc.c (0975)               the probe-time assign above, plus a map_attach double free.
#   iris_vpu_common.c (1099)       power domain dropped after the clocks, AHB bridge reset.
#   dsi_host.c (0410 0420 0430)    a VM leak in dsi_tx_buf_alloc_6g().
#   qcom-ipcc.c (0055)             NULL chan guard + lock in shutdown; 0055 is the IRQ flag.
#   qcom_battmgr.c (0930 0940-0943)  charger supplies notified of online changes.
#   pmic_glink_altmode.c (1044), ucsi.c (1042), pcie-qcom.c + pci-imx6.c (1060 1067),
#   ath12k/wmi.c (1010 1025), arm64 Kconfig/process.c/fault.c + kernel/sys.c (0010 0020 0025),
#   kernel-parameters.txt (1040)   small fixes, none in a hunk of ours.
# Beside us, not intersecting: geni-se firmware-load fixes (every GENI serial engine), mac80211
# frames queued while off-channel, ath11k dp_srng leak, iris/venus iova from the restrict region,
# qcom_smbx (not built here: our SM8250/SM6115 charger is 0910's driver).
#
# PATCHES: all 313 (0896 out) applied cumulatively at --fuzz=0, no rejects. DROP CHECK: 540
# (patch, file) pairs reverse-applied --dry-run --fuzz=0 to pristine 7.3.4: only 0896's reverses.
# Positive control on the patched tree: 464 reverse (the rest are files a later patch edits
# again). ChangeLog subjects vs our patch subjects: 0896 only. CONFIG: all 809 symbols named in
# kernel/*.config exist in the patched tree (CONFIG_x / CONFIG_ARCH_x are comment placeholders).
# BUILD: `make kernel` green on the branch tip (0268/0270/0275 in, 1065 out): vmlinuz.efi + 35 dtbs
# + modules (7.3.4) staged. Warnings only in our own drivers (chipone_tddi, qcom-spmi-haptics,
# rmi4, wcd939x-usbss) and the fragment-comment `.config` noise; none in a file 7.3.4 touched. The
# unshipped-qcom list names no symbol that is new in 7.3.4.
#
# Owed on hardware, besides the series list below: audio on both DSP stacks through a long
# session (q6apm on ACE/S2/FIT/Odin 3, q6asm on Max/Thor Lite/Air Y Pro; listen for a loop or
# stutter at a period boundary, check xruns), SM6115 + SM8250 LPASS clock votes now through
# stable's q6afe, SM8250 ADSP + fastrpc probe clean with 1166 under the probe-time assign (no
# SError at boot), WSA speakers on ACE/S2/FIT with no `ASoC error (-5)`, UFS through suspend on
# an internal install, USB-C alt mode plug/unplug.

# ============================== 7.3.3 ==============================
#
# 7.3.2 carries the content (548 commits); 7.3.3 adds three Xen backend use-after-free fixes.
# 7.3.1 -> 7.3.3 changes 456 files and no Kconfig file. What concerns us: seven ath12k commits
# (RXDMA buffer ring size per memory profile), drm/msm "Fix vm_bo use-after-free in
# with_vm_locks()", three qcom-wled fixes, arm-smmu-v3 shutdown ordering. No qcom clk, phy,
# interconnect, dts or soundwire change.
#
# Intersection with our patches, four files, all read:
#   drm/msm/msm_gem_shrinker.c     upstream walks vm_bos with the _safe variant; our 0220 lands
#                                  elsewhere in the file.
#   ath12k/core.c, core.h, mac.c   the ring-size rework. 1002, 1011, 1025 and 1026 land with
#                                  offsets; WCN7850/7860 take the default memory profile, now
#                                  4096-entry RXDMA buffer rings.
# All 267 patches applied cumulatively at --fuzz=0, no rejects, none reversed;
# kernel/patches/check-order.py: no problems.

# ============================== 7.3.1 ==============================
#
# A series bump, so the stack was rebased rather than re-applied: a git tree of 7.2.11 with one
# commit per patch, rebased onto a 7.3.1 tree, so every hunk got a three-way merge and only real
# conflicts stopped it. Then only the patches whose original no longer produced the same tree were
# regenerated (`git apply --cached`, headers kept). 47 of 269 patches failed a plain --fuzz=0
# apply, most on context only.
#
# Deleted, landed byte-for-byte (their commits went empty in the rebase): 0145 (sm6115 video GDSC
# HW_CTRL), 0230 (Rob Clark's VM hardening), 0620 (sy7758), 0800 (DP audio prepare), 1000 (ksmbd
# pipe transceive), 1063 (qmp-combo runtime PM at boot), 1080 (qce runtime PM), 1155 (sm8650 CPU
# props), 1165 (sm6115 venus), 1167 (sm8750 uart15).
#
# Reworked (each patch header carries a "7.3.1 bump" note):
#   0530  mainline now has its own panel-chipone-icna35xx.c, with per-board compatibles none of
#         our DTs use. Ours is renamed beside it: panel-ddic-icna35xx.c, DRM_PANEL_DDIC_ICNA35XX,
#         driver name panel-ddic-icna35xx. 0531-0533 follow; kernel.config changed with it.
#   0810  deleted (port of Nova-Deck b404b61a). It remapped LPAIF 7 to WSA and masked the WSA2
#         channels for our own topology. Mainline's ayaneo,pocket-s2-sndcard maps the stream onto
#         the WSA2 channels itself. Pocket S2 and Pocket FIT are both that card now, model
#         SM8650-APS2 (set once, in sm8650-ayaneo-common.dtsi), and load
#         qcom/ayaneo-ps2/SM8650-APS2-tplg.bin, built in qcom-firmwares from linux-firmware's
#         topology source. UCM moved from conf.d/sm8650 to conf.d/ayaneo-ps2 and the FIT's card id
#         is SM8650APS2. That topology has no DISPLAY_PORT_RX_0 on MultiMedia1; DP plays on
#         MultiMedia6 / PCM 5.
#   0820, 0825  deleted, replaced by a new 0820 (the MI2S half of b404b61a). Their card-level
#         "i2s_clk" gives way to mainline's per-DAI MI2S clocks: a `bclk` on a dai@<port> node
#         under &q6apmbedai, set and enabled by sc8280xp_snd_hw_params() when the card data has
#         mi2s_bclk_enable. sm8450/sm8550 data already do; the new 0820 sets it for sm8750. Moved:
#         Odin 2 family + RP6/Nova on dai@10 (PRIMARY_MI2S_RX), Odin 3 + FIT Elite on dai@12
#         (SECONDARY_MI2S_RX), RG55G1 + RP Classic on dai@93 (SENARY_MI2S_RX; the sm4450 card uses
#         the sm8450 data). The back end is fixed at 48 kHz / 2 ch / S16, so bclk is 1536000, the
#         rate the old assigned-clock-rates pinned.
#   0826  now only adds to mainline's hw_params: the codec format on every codec DAI of an MI2S
#         link (both SM4450 amps; mainline sets the first only), the RP Classic mono fixup, and a
#         bclk counted over max(channels, 2) slots so the mono stream stays at 1536000. Thor Lite
#         (SM8250) keeps its card clock: it uses sm8250.c, not this driver.
#   0855  the runtime-PM half landed; only the system-sleep handlers are left.
#   0994  extended: 7.3 reads the regulator state back at probe (REG_ENABLE); PBS uses offset 0x0.
#   1090  extended: the IRQ is re-enabled on the new pm_runtime_force_* error returns.
#   0120  upstream dropped skip_retention_level, so our two .skip_retention_level lines went too.
#   0398  sm4450 maps to the new ubwc_2_0_hbb14 preset (same values).
#   1020  follows the pwrseq_power_on/off -> pwrseq_enable/disable rename.
#   1062  re-inserted beside upstream's new sm8475 config.
#   1145  keeps upstream's sm8750 VBIF 0x3000.
#   1105  shrank: 7.3 has the pcie*_port0 labels.
#
# API: of_drm_get_panel_orientation() became drm_of_get_panel_orientation() in <drm/drm_of.h>;
# the 16 panel drivers we add follow it (0505-0590). IIO consumers are in the IIO_CONSUMER
# namespace now, which 0910's pm8150b charger imports.
#
# Duplicate drivers: of every compatible our patches add, only 0540's ayaneo,wt0600-2k and
# ayaneo,wt0630-2k are also matched by a 7.3 driver (panel-renesas-r63419). That driver defaults to
# n and is not in our config, so ours binds. 0515 sits beside st7703 the same way.
#
# DT: sm8550.dtsi renamed pcieport0 to pcie0_port0, and qcs8550-ayn-common.dtsi and
# qcs8550-ayaneo-pocket-common.dtsi follow; sm8250/8650/8750 keep pcieport0. The sm8550 and sm8650
# IPA nodes now reference ipa_fw_mem, a node our three common dtsi files delete (no modem), so they
# drop that property too. IPA stays disabled.
#
# Crypto: CRYPTO_DEV_QCOM_RNG is gone (now HW_RANDOM_QCOM). CRYPTO_DEV_QCE now depends on BROKEN
# (it races the secure world for the engine and is slower than the CPU), so it is deleted from
# kernel.config. The driver going does not take the DT node with it: every SoC's `crypto` node is
# enabled, and on sm8250/8550/8650/8750 it lists interconnects, so with no driver to bind it
# fw_devlink holds the interconnect providers' sync_state forever ("sync_state() pending due to
# 1dfa000.crypto") and every NoC node stays at its maximum vote. Upstream (Nova-Deck 6f40319a) saw
# that break every Odin 3 panel off->on and hang power-off. Every board file that reaches a crypto
# node sets `&crypto { status = "disabled"; }`: upstream's eight, plus sm8250-mangmi-air-y-pro.dts
# and sm6115-mangmi-air-x-base.dtsi. sm4450 has no crypto node. If QCE ever returns, re-enable the
# node with it.
#
# Result: all 259 patches applied cumulatively at --fuzz=0, and the tree was byte-identical to the
# rebased one. `make kernel` green (Image + 32 dtbs + modules); DDIC_ICNA35XX=y, CHIPONE_ICNA35XX
# and RENESAS_R63419 unset, HW_RANDOM_QCOM=y. tests/test-hw-dtb.sh and
# tests/test-panel-calibration.sh green.
#
# Added 2026-11-02: SM8750's share of Abel Vesa's CX v5 (9/42 + 41/42 into 1150, 26/42 into 0142),
# which the SM8750 bring-up missed. Gated the same day on an Odin 3 (upstream's dev card): GCC is a
# consumer of `cx` and runtime-PM active before and after a freeze cycle, no errors, WCN7850
# re-associated. `sync_state() pending due to 3d37000.gmu` for gcc, gpucc and gxclkctl is not from
# this: the GMU node lists GCC_GPU_GEMNOC_GFX_CLK in pristine 7.3.1 and no driver binds it.

# ============================== 7.3.x on hardware ==============================
#
# Seen so far:
#   - 7.3.1, Pocket S2 (2026-10-31): sound came up as Dummy Output until the DP route moved into
#     the APS2 HiFi verb in UCM (8ac2c00d); speaker OK after.
#   - 7.3.1, Air X (2026-11-01): Wi-Fi late or absent, from 7.3's qrtr HELLO change dropping the
#     name service's early answer to the modem. Fixed by 1018.
#   - 7.3.3, card 3a87b3fc (PR #38 comment): boot, Wi-Fi and suspend checked on four boards.
#     ACE: all OK, deep suspend included. Air Y Pro: OK, but the SLPI crashes in its sensor process
#     60 ms after resume and recovers by itself. Air X: the ADSP crashes the same way after resume,
#     no sound card comes back and the device freezes; not attributed to 7.3.3 (nothing in
#     remoteproc, fastrpc, soc/qcom or rpmsg changed since 7.3.1), but 7.3.1 had no suspend run to
#     compare with. RG55G1: OK; three disp_cc byte0/byte0_intf/pclk0 "stuck at 'on'" WARNs, and
#     rtcwake cannot run (the pm8xxx RTC is not a wake source in its DT). S2 not run.
#
# Still owed for the series:
#   - Audio everywhere: MI2S formats and bit clocks now come from mainline (every MI2S speaker
#     board; a "pll lock fail" from an aw88xxx amp means no BCLK), S2 + FIT speakers, headphones
#     and DP, headset jack on MI2S boards (0861).
#   - Display: the ICNA35XX panels (Pocket DS/EVO, Odin 2 Portal, Thor, Odin 3, Pocket Max) bind
#     panel-ddic-icna35xx; SM4450 UBWC through the preset; picture and touch after resume.
#   - PCIe Wi-Fi on the qcs8550 boards (label move), SM6115 Bluetooth (1020), the RNG (hwrng
#     should list qcom).
#   - From 7.2.11, never gated: WCN7850 association, UFS probe clean on an internal install (a
#     dev card boots from SD), a normal boot and Steam session on btrfs.
#   - 0190/0195: a Pocket ACE boot shows 0 `cbfrsynra=0x1c00` faults where it showed 10.
#   - Audio playback, sustained GPU load, and the S2 (bonded panel) on 7.3.3.

# ============================== Running the HW gate (any pin) ==============================
#
# Boards: one per SoC at least, and the ones that are alone in what they exercise:
#   SM8550  Pocket ACE   video-mode panel, WCN7850, pad behind the Renesas PCIe-USB bridge.
#   SM8650  Pocket S2    the only bonded-DSI panel (one 1440x2560 panel over two links); its
#                        1080-line render sits 8 lines under the inline rotator's 1088-line cap,
#                        the tightest display margin we have.
#           Pocket FIT   the only DSC panel.
#   SM8250  Pocket Max   command-mode panel, ath11k Wi-Fi; or Thor Lite / Air Y Pro.
#   SM6115  Air X        ath10k WCN3950, ADSP/modem bring-up.
#   SM4450  RG55G1
#   SM8750  Odin 3       upstream's dev card; we have none.
# Read the node's compatible on the device, not the board name, to know what a board proves: a
# Max pass says nothing about WCN7850, since its Wi-Fi is ath11k (pci17cb,1101).
#
# Flash a card built from the pin. A new Image invalidates the whole /lib/modules/<ver> tree
# (module BTF), so never swap /boot/Image on an existing card.
#
# Video decode: test iris/venus with `ffmpeg -c:v h264_v4l2m2m` on a clip made on the device
# (`ffmpeg -f lavfi -i testsrc=size=1280x720:rate=30:duration=2 ...`), not with Steam. Iris loads
# its firmware at STREAMON and logs nothing on success, so /dev/video0 existing proves nothing;
# the decoded byte count does (1280*720*1.5 per frame).
#
# Logs: /var/log is bind-mounted onto /home (var-log.mount), so on a card read
#   journalctl -D /run/media/<you>/retroforge-home/.retroforge/offload/var/log/journal --list-boots
# and pass a boot ID: `-b -1` does not work with -D ("no persistent journal was found").
#
# KNOWN BOOT NOISE. Before chasing a boot line, grep this file for it.
#   - All boards, on resume: `IRQ168: set affinity failed(-22)`.
#   - synaptics_dsx_i2c "I2C retry 1..10" / "Failed to read interrupt status": touchscreen-driver
#     noise, also while the panel is blanked; not suspend fallout.
#   - `qcom-apm ... CMD timeout for [1001021] opcode` at ~10 s on ACE, FIT and S2, with working
#     audio. Not a no-sound cause.
#   - Pocket S2: `dsi_get_phy: phy driver is not ready` at ~1 s (probe deferral on the secondary
#     DSI), and `soundwire sdw-master-2-0: clock stop deprepare wait failed:-110` after the card
#     is up. A first boot with no sound card at all is the SM8650 SoundWire wedge, issue #105;
#     a reboot brings it back.
#   - SM8250 (Max, Air Y Pro): a clk_core_disable + clk_core_unprepare WARNING pair after the
#     boot-time `DSI PLL(0) lock failed`, since 7.2.
#   - Pocket ACE: 10 arm-smmu context faults at ~0.77 s, all fsr=0x402 cbfrsynra=0x1c00 (the MDSS
#     stream), before the panel rails come up: the bootloader splash still scanning out into an
#     empty translating domain, before 0370 can stop it. Other boards show none. 0190 (SM8550) and
#     0195 (SM8650) give MDSS an identity domain at boot and should take it to 0 (owed, above).

# ============================== Bumping the pin (any pin) ==============================
#
# Run these in order; each catches what the others cannot.
#
# 1. Upstream intersection, first. Take the `+++ b/` paths out of the release's incremental patch
#    (https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v7.x/incr/patch-A-B.xz) and intersect them with the
#    `+++ b/` paths in kernel/patches/*.patch. Read every file it names and answer two questions:
#    did upstream break one of ours, and did one of ours land (then it is a deletion candidate).
#    It is the only offline check that sees upstream's own changes: at 7.2.5 neither the patch
#    apply nor the config sweep could see the DSI break.
#
# 2. Changes beside our patches. The intersection cannot see drivers we depend on but do not
#    patch. Scan the ChangeLog for i2c/qcom-geni and soc/qcom/geni-se (every touchscreen, panel
#    rail and amp is behind GENI), drm/msm, ath10k/11k/12k and mac80211, ASoC qcom and soundwire,
#    media/qcom/iris, remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas, pcie-qcom, usb typec/ucsi, btrfs, and record
#    what each pin's legs are, so the next reader knows they were looked at.
#
# 3. Patch apply. All of kernel/patches/*.patch, cumulatively, in lexical order, onto one pristine
#    tree, at --fuzz=0 (as build.sh does). Applying each patch alone to a pristine tree reports
#    false failures: several patches patch files an earlier one creates, and the panel patches all
#    extend one Makefile. For a series bump, rebase instead (see 7.3.1 above).
#
# 4. Drop check. A clean apply proves nothing about what landed upstream:
#    - reverse-apply each patch with --dry-run --fuzz=0 to a pristine tree, file by file; a file
#      that reverses cleanly has landed;
#    - GNU patch skips the whole file at the first reversed hunk and then reports "N out of N
#      hunks ignored", which reads as "all upstream" and may be false. Count the call sites in the
#      pristine tree instead;
#    - `patch --batch` silently applies a reversed patch, i.e. reverts upstream's fix. Use -N
#      when asking whether a patch is still needed;
#    - "mainline does not have this line" does not mean mainline removed it: check whether the
#      function still exists, and if not, where its callers went;
#    - for every patch you changed or whose file upstream touched, grep the patched tree for an
#      identifier it introduces.
#
# 5. Patches carried from a list: check the author, not the thread. Look up the author's other
#    postings (`b4 mbox <msgid>` reads a thread; patchwork's
#    /api/1.2/patches/?submitter=<id>&per_page=100 lists an author, the id coming from
#    /api/1.2/patches/?msgid=<msgid>). A patch its author has superseded looks exactly like one
#    awaiting review: one message, no replies, state `new`. The supersession is in another thread.
#    It is a reason not to carry a patch, not a forecast that it will not land: the old 0508 was
#    superseded by its author and the maintainer merged it anyway, in 7.2.8.
#    patchwork's `handled-elsewhere` means another project owns the row, not "applied".
#    lore's HTML and search are behind Anubis (HTTP 403); `b4 am -o <dir> <msgid>` and
#    /all/<msgid>/t.mbox.gz are not, and b4 applies the list's trailers. Patchwork's JSON API also
#    works (/api/1.2/series/<sid>/, /patches/<id>/ with a byte-exact `diff`, /covers/<id>/), but
#    its mbox and raw endpoints 404, and a 0/N cover letter is not indexed as a patch.
#
# 6. Config. Every CONFIG_* named in kernel/*.config must exist in the patched tree (some come
#    from our patches, e.g. AYANEO_SERIAL_MCU from 0980). Then merge the fragments for real
#    (`merge_config.sh -m defconfig kernel/*.config` + `make olddefconfig`) and assert every
#    requested value against the final .config: olddefconfig silently drops a =y whose
#    dependencies are unmet. Strip trailing whitespace and inline comments before comparing. A
#    trim directive that comes back undefined rather than `n` is cut by another symbol and the
#    line can go; build.sh lists those as redundant. DEBUG_INFO_BTF and SCHED_CLASS_EXT need the
#    container's pahole (dwarves).
#
# 7. Build. `make kernel`, and record the warnings by file: warnings in our own drivers cannot be
#    bump fallout, warnings in files the release touched can be.
#
# 8. Hardware, as above. Then record the pin in the history list and a section for it here.
#
# Config renames from 7.1.5, still current in kernel.config (do not restore the old names):
#   CRYPTO_MICHAEL_MIC dropped (removed upstream; mac80211 has its own michael_mic),
#   MFD_QCOM_SPMI_PMIC -> MFD_SPMI_PMIC, PHY_QCOM_SNPS_EUSB2 -> PHY_SNPS_EUSB2 (+
#   PHY_QCOM_EUSB2_REPEATER), SM_DISPCC_8650 -> SM_DISPCC_8550 (SM8650 reuses the 8550 dispcc).
#   READ_ONLY_THP_FOR_FS was removed in 7.2 (file THP is unconditional).

# ============================== Standing notes ==============================
#
# 0330, Dmitry Baryshkov's "drm/msm: fix SMMU fault dumps" (v4 since 2026-10-12): exercised at
# 7.2.10 by three manual KMS blank cycles each on ACE, S2 and Max (`gamescopectl
# drm_sleep_internal_screen 1/0`; retroforge-suspend does not reach that path, it falls back to
# bl_power). Pocket FIT, the DSC board, is still owed. It removes the kernel's allow_modeset
# override, so enabling colour management needs a commit with DRM_MODE_ATOMIC_ALLOW_MODESET; see
# the patch's preamble for what that means for gamescope.
#
# LUTDMA (0360, 0365, 1145): a port of the downstream SDE reg-dma engine. On DPU 9.0 and later the
# colour LUTs have no memory-mapped write path, which is why mainline exposes only CTM and
# GAMMA_LUT there. The engine drives the DSPP inverse gamma (a 256-entry DEGAMMA_LUT) and the
# 17^3 gamut block (a DPU_3D_LUT blob); without its reg entry the properties are not exposed.
# HW-verified 2026-09-13/14 on FIT (engine v3), S2 and ACE (engine v2). A failed LUTDMA wait skips
# that DSPP while the commit still reports success, bounded by a retry budget on the CRTC: that is
# the failure to watch for on new silicon.
#
# What 7.2 took over from us: the sm8550 DDR/LLCC/L3 bandwidth scaling (verbatim) and the sgm3804
# panel-power regulator, which landed as a rewrite with a different binding: two rails from
# `pos`/`neg` child nodes with `enable-gpios`, where ours was one rail. All six board nodes and
# their panels were migrated: `avdd-supply` is the positive rail and every panel driver takes an
# `avee` supply too; the rails are pinned at 5200000 uV, the voltage our old driver actually wrote
# (asking for 5.0 V would be a real change); each rail has a 40 ms enable_time. Cross-checked
# against Neil Armstrong's Pocket S2 display series (vin-supply = <&vph_pwr>,
# regulator-active-discharge, regulator-boot-on added). HW-checked on Pocket ACE, Pocket S2 and
# Pocket FIT; Pocket DMG, DS, S1K and S2K are untested, and a lit backlight over a black panel
# (AVEE dead) is the failure to look for.
# Upstream names those rails vsp/vsn and drives the S2 panel with panel-renesas-r63419, which 7.3
# has but we do not enable. If we switch to it, the DTS supply names must change with it.
